 "phase": "L1 (loading time): the loading-file streams changed in place",
 "change": "OriginalLoadingFiles.character, scannerAccess and write change their stream in place in the streams dictionary (Dictionary.Values index) instead of copying the whole Stream (its raw, input, output and pending byte arrays and strings) out and back for every character; decodeDAT runs its 123-byte header, character, scanf-lookahead and write steps on the two streams held locally and stores them back before the closes; one decoded byte no longer allocates a one-element array. Every observe event, its order and arguments, and every value left after success or a throw are those of the old code. The started and loaded events carry uptime (telemetry for load_memory.py).",
 "profile": "A12 load profile ml-p0-loadprof (simpleperf DWARF, 12,308 main-thread samples over the load): catalog session 49% (object consume 32%, sheet finishing 19% with array copies 9.7%, decodeDAT 16%, frame bodies 9.5%), catalog package read+verify 25% (portable SHA-256 15%, Bitmap.init 8.8%), arena package 2.5%; the load is CPU-bound on the main thread (131 s on-CPU by the loaded event of 135 s since start). Mac sample: decodeDAT 38% of the load, three quarters of it Stream copies and destroys.",
 "review": "independent read-only reviewer: no behavioural difference (events, values after success and every throw, exclusivity and Dictionary index validity); follow-ups: rename the decodeDAT local that hid the source parameter, strengthen the per-byte partial-write case of the new test (both carried into L2)",
 "notes": "Baseline noise (ml-p0, three unprofiled runs): A12 load 122.1-123.25 s, startup 2.89-2.94 s; Mac 5.05-5.39 s. A12 RSS varies with zram swap (VmHWM 1109-1550 MB over identical runs, swap 190-250 MB); VmRSS+VmSwap (peakFootprintMB) is stable within 20 MB and is the memory metric.",
